A||||13||88formula||ATTENTION 3.4 FIEROS||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||06-29-2000||05:32 PM||||I want to know what you guys get for 1/4-mile times and your gas mileage with your 3.4 fieros. I have the chance to pick up a 3.4 with 50,000 miles for $500. My car will be a daily driver so that is why I am concerned about the gas mileage. With the 2.8 I got no worse than 24 mpg and 29 on the highway.<P>If I get the 3.4 I will sell my 2.8 with 50,000 miles on it. I have all the service records for the motor since it was new. I don't know what I will sell it for yet.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fret Naught||06-29-2000||05:43 PM||||Will that 3.4 drop right in? or are there major Mods involved? what kind of H.P. increase do you expect to get? I have my eyes on one as well||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||06-29-2000||06:30 PM||||The 3.4 will bolt right in provided you relocate the starter to the other side of the block, which means you have to drill. You have to get a neutrally balanced flywheel for it for the manual transmission unless you have an 88 v6 2.8. You have to fabricate a front motor mount for it on the 88's from an 85-87 model that has something to do with the AC bracket. You have to grind away a flange on the bell housing of the motor for automatic transmission models so that it will bolt up.<P>I hear 180 HP with stock everything and 200-210 with cam, ported heads, and ported manifolds. The real nice torque curve though is what sets you back in your seat and this motor has what it takes to do that. The 2.8 is kind of weak in the torque curve area considering how heavy a fiero is.<P>Check this info out and learn what I did.  <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/Page1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/Page1.html</A>  <A HREF="http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/engine/engine.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/engine/engine.html</A> <BR>And don’t forget this one, <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/e-conv.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/e-conv.htm</A>  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||06-29-2000||07:30 PM||||My 3.4 with a 4.10 four speed gets 21 MPG in town. It is not a highway car, so I cant help you on that mileage, but with a 5-speed mileage should be really close to the 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||06-29-2000||08:13 PM||||I'm thinking about buying another fiero and putting a 3.4 in or if i get a gt put a 3.4 in my coupe.some one give it a difficulty rating from 1-10 1 being easiest. I would rate changing clutch on my 87 4cyl as a 6   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> just kidding.<BR>I am some what mechanical. But still only a First timer.<p>[This message has been edited by zeusrekning (edited 06-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroshop||06-29-2000||11:34 PM||||Having installed several 3.4 I can honestly say that they are a better motor then the 2.8. I have the 2.8 in my 88GT and when that goes out I will install a 3.4 and of course a few little extras thown in for better performance. At this time I have 5 Fieros waiting for the 3.4 install.||||reg||10
Z||000006||Alex4mula||06-30-2000||02:56 PM||||My 3.4 is giving me around 20 MPG but I have a concrete block foot :-) No 1/4 mi yet. Looking for Dyno & further tuning.||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||06-30-2000||04:47 PM||||It's getting close to the answer here but no cigar yet. Thanks for your reply guys/girls.||||reg||1
