Z||000012||Black88GT||07-05-2000||01:01 PM||||I will be doing this swap in my Fiero shortly with the much much much needed help of mike lecompte.  Recently I asked this same question to a guy I talked to with a 94 Firebird 3.4 5 speed.  He said he can get up to 27 mpg highway and around 22 mpg city.  This is better then my crappy old 2.8 was getting, and the firebird is a lot heavier.  I think bang for the buck wise and ease of installation this is a very good swap.  I also heard that the 2.8 was flawed, something to do with oil flow.  About the brackets and stuff needed, I just talked to ed parks and he sells everything for like 75 bucks if you give him your old stuff back, if not 100 bucks.  He said he just ran out of one of the brackets (my luck) so I guess I will have to figure that one out.  I believe stock the engine is 160 Hp and 200 lb. ft. torque.  I forget what the RPM was but I think it was higher then the 2.8. I figure with ported manifolds, no cat., new fiero store intake, power pulley, few other little things here and there, and 200 Hp is my goal (reasonable). It will be under 1600 for everything too.  Compare that to a 3.8 swap, that won't even buy you the engine.   <P>just my 2 cents...||||reg||14
Z||000013||88formula||07-05-2000||10:40 PM||||Black88GT, read your E-mail.||||reg||1
